1
00:00:02,439 --> 00:00:05,168
So by now, we learned about the difference

2
00:00:05,168 --> 00:00:05,955
between real

3
00:00:06,693 --> 00:00:09,646
objects and data containers, and we learned

4
00:00:09,646 --> 00:00:12,712
that polymorphism is one important aspect

5
00:00:12,712 --> 00:00:15,248
that we can keep in mind when we work with

6
00:00:15,265 --> 00:00:18,379
classes to avoid code duplication and

7
00:00:18,491 --> 00:00:21,155
therefore to stay DRY, which ultimately is a

8
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:23,435
part of writing clean, readable, and

9
00:00:23,531 --> 00:00:24,350
maintainable code.

10
00:00:25,072 --> 00:00:27,528
Now I wanna have a closer look at classes in

11
00:00:27,624 --> 00:00:30,610
general, no matter if we use polymorphism or

12
00:00:30,610 --> 00:00:33,304
not. How do you write clean classes in

13
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:33,961
general?

14
00:00:34,682 --> 00:00:37,295
Let's say you're writing some new class for

15
00:00:37,503 --> 00:00:40,261
whichever data entity you might have and how

16
00:00:40,389 --> 00:00:41,800
should you now write this class?

17
00:00:43,114 --> 00:00:45,647
Well, clean classes should be small,

18
00:00:46,224 --> 00:00:48,292
just like functions in the end.

19
00:00:49,029 --> 00:00:52,027
You typically should prefer multiple smaller

20
00:00:52,235 --> 00:00:55,425
classes over a few large classes.

21
00:00:56,499 --> 00:00:58,727
And of course, that is very similar to what

22
00:00:58,727 --> 00:01:00,074
we learned about functions.

23
00:01:00,651 --> 00:01:03,104
Clean functions also should be

24
00:01:03,937 --> 00:01:06,166
they should be short, they should be focused

25
00:01:06,262 --> 00:01:09,902
on one thing, as you learned, to ensure that

26
00:01:09,902 --> 00:01:12,803
not too many lines of code are in one

27
00:01:12,932 --> 00:01:15,705
function and to ensure that they are always

28
00:01:16,122 --> 00:01:17,790
easy to comprehend and read.

29
00:01:18,688 --> 00:01:20,900
And it's the same here for classes now.

30
00:01:21,493 --> 00:01:23,898
However, there is an important difference

31
00:01:24,155 --> 00:01:27,169
when we define what small means exactly.

32
00:01:27,826 --> 00:01:31,001
With functions, we had the concept of a

33
00:01:31,129 --> 00:01:32,524
function doing one thing. Thing,

34
00:01:33,118 --> 00:01:35,718
with classes, we have a related yet

35
00:01:35,862 --> 00:01:36,905
different concept.

36
00:01:37,531 --> 00:01:40,484
Classes should have a single responsibility.

37
00:01:41,544 --> 00:01:44,561
And there is a principle, a well-known

38
00:01:44,689 --> 00:01:45,331
principle,

39
00:01:46,118 --> 00:01:49,247
the Single Responsibility Principle, which

40
00:01:49,247 --> 00:01:51,285
actually also revolves around that.

41
00:01:51,815 --> 00:01:54,206
And I will come back to that principle in

42
00:01:54,222 --> 00:01:55,330
just a second again.

43
00:01:55,908 --> 00:01:58,427
The general idea simply is that a product

44
00:01:58,427 --> 00:02:01,108
class, for example, should be responsible

45
00:02:01,140 --> 00:02:04,172
for product-related issues, for example,

46
00:02:04,252 --> 00:02:06,787
changing the name of a product, not for

47
00:02:06,995 --> 00:02:09,498
changing the name of a user, for example.

48
00:02:09,963 --> 00:02:13,203
This might sound trivial, but it is easy to

49
00:02:13,219 --> 00:02:15,898
mix up these different concepts in reality.

50
00:02:16,781 --> 00:02:19,636
Take this dummy online shop class, for

51
00:02:19,668 --> 00:02:20,262
example.

52
00:02:21,016 --> 00:02:23,438
All the real code is missing, but you can

53
00:02:23,438 --> 00:02:27,128
see the API, the methods, the surface area

54
00:02:27,352 --> 00:02:30,416
of this class here. And you see I got 3

55
00:02:30,481 --> 00:02:31,251
properties here,

56
00:02:31,844 --> 00:02:34,395
orders, offered products, customers,

57
00:02:34,988 --> 00:02:36,625
whichever data would be stored in there

58
00:02:36,673 --> 00:02:38,822
doesn't matter. The names give us a good

59
00:02:38,822 --> 00:02:40,106
idea of what is in there.

60
00:02:40,747 --> 00:02:43,346
And then we have a bunch of methods here for

61
00:02:43,475 --> 00:02:45,704
adding a product, for creating a customer,

62
00:02:45,801 --> 00:02:46,394
and so on.

63
00:02:47,341 --> 00:02:49,827
And all these methods kind of make sense,

64
00:02:49,972 --> 00:02:52,506
right? It's the online shop class after all.

65
00:02:52,795 --> 00:02:54,961
So it makes sense that we can add both a

66
00:02:54,961 --> 00:02:57,370
product as well as add a customer.

67
00:02:58,494 --> 00:03:01,386
But the problem here is not necessarily the

68
00:03:01,386 --> 00:03:02,719
number of methods.

69
00:03:03,378 --> 00:03:05,306
It could make sense to have that many

70
00:03:05,306 --> 00:03:06,607
methods in a class,

71
00:03:07,249 --> 00:03:09,643
but the focus of this class, the

72
00:03:09,643 --> 00:03:11,314
responsibility of this class,

73
00:03:12,133 --> 00:03:14,623
that's the problem. Because this class

74
00:03:14,639 --> 00:03:17,258
doesn't just have one responsibility.

75
00:03:17,756 --> 00:03:20,470
Instead, this class is dealing with orders,

76
00:03:20,744 --> 00:03:23,361
with products, with customers, And even

77
00:03:23,393 --> 00:03:25,044
there, it's actually having multiple

78
00:03:25,140 --> 00:03:25,685
purposes.

79
00:03:26,262 --> 00:03:28,826
It is dealing with updating and adding

80
00:03:28,922 --> 00:03:31,631
products and removing products, but then it

81
00:03:31,631 --> 00:03:33,939
also is responsible for restocking a

82
00:03:33,971 --> 00:03:37,161
product, which is not the same as changing a

83
00:03:37,161 --> 00:03:38,395
product name in the end.

84
00:03:38,940 --> 00:03:40,799
So this class has a bunch of

85
00:03:40,847 --> 00:03:43,187
responsibilities, at least 3,

86
00:03:43,812 --> 00:03:46,217
orders, products, and customers, but maybe

87
00:03:46,313 --> 00:03:47,210
even more than that.

88
00:03:47,739 --> 00:03:48,990
And that would be a problem here.

89
00:03:49,583 --> 00:03:52,373
Even if every method would just have one

90
00:03:52,645 --> 00:03:53,335
line of code.

91
00:03:53,993 --> 00:03:56,496
Then this class wouldn't be big when we

92
00:03:56,496 --> 00:03:59,786
count lines of code, but it would be big if

93
00:03:59,786 --> 00:04:01,759
we consider its responsibilities.

94
00:04:02,658 --> 00:04:05,354
And a better way to write this code would be

95
00:04:05,386 --> 00:04:08,804
to split this class into multiple smaller

96
00:04:08,852 --> 00:04:10,119
classes, for example.

97
00:04:11,018 --> 00:04:13,441
And this is just one possible split here, of

98
00:04:13,505 --> 00:04:13,810
course.

99
00:04:14,387 --> 00:04:17,003
Here we could have classes which do have

100
00:04:17,195 --> 00:04:19,089
separate responsibilities.

101
00:04:19,922 --> 00:04:22,390
Again, you might even be able to split this

102
00:04:22,470 --> 00:04:25,212
up further, but you can already see the idea

103
00:04:25,276 --> 00:04:28,225
here. We have multiple smaller classes

104
00:04:28,818 --> 00:04:32,121
where small really means that we have less

105
00:04:32,329 --> 00:04:35,279
responsibilities in our individual classes.

106
00:04:35,776 --> 00:04:39,110
And this is considered clean code. Small

107
00:04:39,543 --> 00:04:40,970
focused classes

108
00:04:41,563 --> 00:04:43,855
where I know that if I wanna change

109
00:04:43,951 --> 00:04:46,454
something on the product logic, I have to go

110
00:04:46,454 --> 00:04:47,545
to the Product class

111
00:04:48,283 --> 00:04:50,305
and I don't have to scroll through the

112
00:04:50,305 --> 00:04:53,547
entire large class here just to find the

113
00:04:53,675 --> 00:04:55,922
product-specific functions I'm looking for.

114
00:04:57,109 --> 00:04:59,677
That's the idea behind small classes and

115
00:04:59,757 --> 00:05:01,763
what you should focus on when writing

116
00:05:01,843 --> 00:05:02,357
classes.

117
00:05:02,966 --> 00:05:03,817
Keep them small

118
00:05:04,411 --> 00:05:06,513
and define small by looking at their

119
00:05:06,513 --> 00:05:07,524
responsibilities.

120
00:05:08,663 --> 00:05:11,809
I absolutely wanna highlight that small for

121
00:05:11,953 --> 00:05:15,865
classes unlike for functions, does not mean

122
00:05:16,218 --> 00:05:17,629
do just one thing.

123
00:05:18,206 --> 00:05:20,851
This Product class knows how to update and

124
00:05:20,947 --> 00:05:23,399
remove, for example, which is definitely

125
00:05:23,415 --> 00:05:24,746
more than one thing,

126
00:05:25,339 --> 00:05:27,760
but it's the same responsibility. The

127
00:05:27,760 --> 00:05:31,190
responsibility is to manage the product data

128
00:05:31,190 --> 00:05:33,354
and the product existence. That's the

129
00:05:33,354 --> 00:05:34,508
responsibility here.

130
00:05:35,454 --> 00:05:37,265
And that's a core difference to functions.

131
00:05:38,003 --> 00:05:40,039
And this difference, of course, makes sense

132
00:05:40,343 --> 00:05:42,411
because if we would have the same definition

133
00:05:42,491 --> 00:05:45,394
as for functions, then every class would in

134
00:05:45,394 --> 00:05:48,076
the end only be allowed to have exactly one

135
00:05:48,349 --> 00:05:51,080
method, right? And if you create one class

136
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:53,682
per method, then this is definitely not

137
00:05:53,682 --> 00:05:56,412
efficient and you would end up with dozens

138
00:05:56,460 --> 00:05:59,721
of super tiny classes which probably then

139
00:05:59,914 --> 00:06:01,424
also would have strange names

140
00:06:02,162 --> 00:06:04,331
just to have one method per class.

141
00:06:04,973 --> 00:06:07,174
This makes no sense at all. It basically

142
00:06:07,302 --> 00:06:10,000
defeats the idea of using classes in the

143
00:06:10,032 --> 00:06:10,659
first place.

144
00:06:11,564 --> 00:06:14,121
So it's not about doing just one thing, it

145
00:06:14,170 --> 00:06:17,326
is about having one responsibility per

146
00:06:17,326 --> 00:06:17,698
class.
